  "term": "predisposing cause",
  "definition": "In this historical source, a predisposing cause is an earlier influence that makes a condition more likely, especially an inherited or family-related weakness that sets the stage for later problems. It is described as distinct from an inducing cause, which brings the condition into evident form.",
